# ==============================================================================
# BAOBAB Enterprise Platform
# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore List
#
# File: .trivyignore
#
# Purpose
# -------
# Every entry below was investigated individually and confirmed, as of the
# date noted, to have NO available fix in any release we can install —
# not "we haven't gotten to it yet," but "we checked, and there is
# currently nothing to upgrade to." Nothing is ignored here on the basis
# of "probably fine" or to make the Trivy gate pass faster.
#
# Each entry has an `exp:` date. When it passes, Trivy stops ignoring that
# ID and the CVE gate fails again on the next scan — deliberately: this is
# a forcing function to re-check upstream rather than let a suppression
# persist forever unreviewed. If upstream still hasn't shipped a fix by
# then, re-verify and extend the date; if they have, remove the entry and
# let the version bump land normally as part of config/resolve.sh's
# normal "latest" tracking.
#
# All four investigated 2026-08-10, in .github/workflows/publish.yml's
# "Scan built container with Trivy" step (Ubuntu 26.04 base image, amd64
# and arm64, config/versions.lock as resolved at that time).
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-56852 — golang.org/x/text: Denial of Service via invalid UTF-8 input
#
# Found in: usr/local/bin/task, usr/local/bin/yq, usr/local/bin/cosign
# Fixed in: golang.org/x/text 0.39.0
#
# All three binaries are official upstream GitHub release binaries,
# compiled by their own maintainers against whatever golang.org/x/text
# version they'd vendored at release time — not something our own
# version-pinning can reach independently of an upstream rebuild.
# Live-checked against the latest available tag of each project
# (go-task/task v3.52.0, mikefarah/yq v4.53.3, sigstore/cosign v3.1.3 —
# all identical to what we already have; no newer release exists for any
# of the three as of this date).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-56852 exp:2026-11-10

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf — gRPC-Go: xDS RBAC and HTTP/2 vulnerabilities
#
# Found in: usr/local/bin/task, usr/local/bin/cosign
# Fixed in: google.golang.org/grpc 1.82.1
#
# Same situation as CVE-2026-56852 above: vendored at compile time by
# task/cosign's own maintainers, in the same latest-available releases
# checked above.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf exp:2026-11-10

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-39822 — Go stdlib os.Root: symlink following allows directory
# traversal
#
# Found in: usr/local/bin/task, usr/local/bin/yq, usr/local/bin/cosign,
#           usr/libexec/docker/cli-plugins/docker-compose
# Fixed in: Go stdlib 1.25.12, 1.26.5, or 1.27.0-rc.2
#
# This is the Go toolchain version each binary was COMPILED WITH, baked in
# at build time — not a dependency any of these projects declare or can
# bump independently of rebuilding with a newer Go release themselves.
# Same latest-available-release check as above applies to task/yq/cosign;
# docker-compose checked separately below.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-11-10

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-34040 — Moby (github.com/docker/docker): Authorization bypass
# vulnerability
#
# Found in: usr/libexec/docker/cli-plugins/docker-buildx,
#           usr/libexec/docker/cli-plugins/docker-compose
# Fixed in: github.com/docker/docker 29.3.1
#
# Confirmed by direct go.mod inspection (not just "no newer tag exists"):
# even the latest available upstream releases — docker/buildx v0.36.1 and
# docker/compose v5.4.0, both newer than what we currently install — still
# declare `github.com/docker/docker v28.5.2+incompatible`, the exact
# vulnerable version. Neither project has adopted the 29.x line in any
# released version yet. Nothing our own apt install of these plugins can
# do about this until they do.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-34040 exp:2026-11-10
